# H-ES3 A/B (D-CAW-MKDIR-LOOKUP-ESTALE-TYPEFLIP-UNRESOLVED): a lookup whose
# poisoned shell could not be retired reads the parent again instead of
# failing -ESTALE (switch poison_unretired_relookup, 1 default, 0 = control).
#
# Measured on the 0.90.131 release build, 4/disk/caw/mpath (g4b): every node of
# path_failover, path_fabric and path_flap logged 1-3 'mutex ERR ESTALE' from
# the workload's shared LOCK directory, each ending on P34H-POISON-UNRETIRED +
# P-LKERR stage=3 err=-116 (or P201-TYPEFLIP-UNRESOLVED-FAIL), and
# path_mount_degraded read two files back ESTALE.  Those rows require zero
# failed operations, so the board fails while this stands.
#
# Build: the main tree's mxfs.ko carrying the switch (modinfo -F srcversion
# mxfs.ko, recorded by each lap's prep).  4/disk/caw/mpath on g4 (test3..test6),
# which overlaps no group in use; every lap on a fresh prep (module load resets
# every knob and capped probe), the switch set by --knobs on every row and read
# back by the row (knobs.txt).  Arms alternate C (0) / F (1), 3 each.
#
# READING RULES (written before the first lap), per lap, from the three rows'
# load_test<N>/ops.log, verify_*.txt and kmsg_test<N>_fromnode.gz (lap_chain
# laps keeps them, PF_KEEP_KMSG=1):
#   ESTALE   'mutex ERR ESTALE' lines over all nodes and rows, plus
#            read_error=ESTALE in verify files.
#   UNRET    P34H-POISON-UNRETIRED lines; RELK P201-RELOOKUP why=poison-unretired.
#   LKERR    P-LKERR stage=3 err=-116 lines.
#   C lap: CONTROL REACH if UNRET >= 1 with an LKERR -116 following it.
#   F lap: FIX if every UNRET is followed (same ino, same comm) by RELK and no
#          LKERR -116 attributable to the poison route; the lap's ESTALE from
#          that route is 0.
#   SUPPORTED: >= 2 C laps with CONTROL REACH, every F lap FIX, and the F laps'
#              total ESTALE below the C laps'.
#   REFUTED:   an F lap whose relookups (3 in one lookup) end in -116 from this
#              arm, or F laps' ESTALE rate equal to the C laps'.
#   Any shutdown, BUG, Oops, hung task, chk/verify bad bytes: attributed from
#   its own lines first; a row's other verdicts are recorded, not graded.
#
# Bounds: prep_cluster 300 s + path_failover 300 + path_fabric 300 +
# path_flap 300 (the manifest budgets) + the chain's overhead outside the
# rows, measured 130-160 s = 1360 s.
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purc1 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=0" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purf1 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=1" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purc2 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=0" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purf2 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=1" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purc3 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=0" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
1360 tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh laps 4/disk/caw/mpath g4 purf3 1 --prep --knobs "poison_unretired_relookup=1" --rows path_failover,path_fabric,path_flap
